    <div class="msg-payload">
      
          <pre class="wordwrap">Hi Siyu, Aleksandr,

Thank you both. -02 takes up your suggestions:

  *
Entity Type is now conditional: needed when the client has to tell
     *
kinds of AI resource apart to choose its next step, and usually
implied by the carrier, such as a well-known name, or by the
Endpoint purpose (Sections 7 and 8.2).
  *
A protocols value can name a version of the agent protocol; where
     *
it does not, the binding states how the client learns which version
to use (Sections 8.2 and 9).
  *
Next to Freshness: a version need not change when a description
     *
changes, while the digest of a description Endpoint does
(Section 8.2).

Aleksandr, the mapping to draft-artamokhov-dawn-marketplace-discovery
is a useful check that the elements fit a deployed discovery document.

-02: <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-cui-dawn-mdi-model/" rel="nofollow">https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-cui-dawn-mdi-model/</a>

Best,
Chenguang

________________________________
发件人: Александр Артамохов &lt;alexar76@rambler.ru&gt;
发送时间: 2026年11月2日 16:14
收件人: <a href="mailto:bhsdfbhsdf@126.com">bhsdfbhsdf@126.com</a> &lt;bhsdfbhsdf@126.com&gt;; <a href="mailto:du_chenguang@outlook.com">du_chenguang@outlook.com</a> &lt;du_chenguang@outlook.com&gt;
抄送: <a href="mailto:dawn@ietf.org">dawn@ietf.org</a> &lt;dawn@ietf.org&gt;
主题: RE: [Dawn] How should we determine the minimum public discovery information?

Hi Siyu,

One data point for your suggestion. The discovery document in draft-artamokhov-dawn-marketplace-discovery has no type field, and the clients that read it have not needed one. The well-known name already says the document describes a catalog, and each URL says its purpose by its member name: catalogue_url continues discovery, manifest_url is a description, mcp_endpoint is for interaction. So the condition could be &quot;required unless the carrier or the Endpoint purpose already implies it&quot;.

A related observation on Endpoint purposes, from reading robots.txt this morning. Of 33,520 remote MCP endpoints (33,469 of them from the official MCP registry, as listed on 26 October), the site&#x27;s own robots.txt disallows the MCP path for automated clients on 4,708 (14%). Of the 4,359 sites involved, 103 explicitly allow a server-card path in the same file, and 680 serve a server card at a path their robots.txt leaves open. So the description and the interaction endpoint of the same entity can carry different access rules. I am not proposing text for this yet.

I can share the counts and the scripts if useful.

Best,
Aleksandr
02.11.2026, 04:33, bhsdfbhsdf &lt;bhsdfbhsdf@126.com&lt;mailto:bhsdfbhsdf@126.com&gt;&gt;
Hi Chenguang,


One small comment on Entity Type in Section 13: I think it could be made conditional.

Suppose an agent and a catalog both provide a description URL. If the client&#x27;s next step is just to fetch the description, it doesn&#x27;t need to know which kind of resource it has found yet.
Could Entity Type be required only when the client needs that distinction to choose its next step?

Best regards,
Siyu Deng



At 2026-11-01 16:54:07, &quot;Du Chenguang&quot; &lt;du_chenguang@outlook.com&gt; wrote:

Hi all,

The charter asks DAWN to specify the minimum public discovery
information, and how we decide what belongs in it seems worth
discussing early. In draft-cui-dawn-mdi-model-01 we made a first
attempt: for each of the charter&#x27;s three deployment contexts, we
asked what a client needs to use a discovery result (choose one,
fetch its description, talk to it, or ask a catalog for more), and
treated only that as the minimum.

<a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-cui-dawn-mdi-model/" rel="nofollow">https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-cui-dawn-mdi-model/</a>

We would welcome your views on whether this is a reasonable way to
determine the minimum, what other approaches we should consider, and
whether the resulting elements match your mechanisms and use cases.

Best,
Chenguang


_______________________________________________
Dawn mailing list -- [/compose]dawn@ietf.org
To unsubscribe send an email to [/compose]dawn-leave@ietf.org

</pre>

      
